      "text": "Proposition A.2. Let q > n , let Ω ⊂ R n be an open bounded connected set, and let u ∈ W 3 ,q (Ω) be a function such that for some positive constant k",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "formula",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.36080815126050414,
        "y0": 0.1399554483372921,
        "x1": 0.6393655978151259,
        "y1": 0.15556719121140142
      },
      "text": "",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.13169828571428552,
        "y0": 0.16974175475059386,
        "x1": 0.8671673862047277,
        "y1": 0.20088761876484562
      },
      "text": "Assume in addition that d ( u -1 (0) , ∂ Ω) > 0 . Let u j ∈ C 2 ,α (Ω) be a sequence of functions such that",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "formula",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.4461184537815124,
        "y0": 0.19930764251781463,
        "x1": 0.5544576569747897,
        "y1": 0.22096544833729223
      },
      "text": "",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1302865210084032,
        "y0": 0.2277463865795724,
        "x1": 0.8671883721660323,
        "y1": 0.26243800178147275
      },
      "text": "Then for every j large enough u -1 j (0) is a C 1 ,s hypersurface, with s = 1 -n/q , and there exist deformations Φ j ∈ W 2 ,q (Ω; R n ) such that",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "list",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1492436806722688,
        "y0": 0.27292474762470303,
        "x1": 0.40611138890756293,
        "y1": 0.28908859560570077
      },
      "text": "(i) Φ j are orthogonal to u -1 (0) ;",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "formula",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.14379816806722684,
        "y0": 0.29900528206650834,
        "x1": 0.39734722638650427,
        "y1": 0.31773462885985754
      },
      "text": "",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "list",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1381509243697479,
        "y0": 0.3285834393111639,
        "x1": 0.2957551757983193,
        "y1": 0.34908859560570077
      },
      "text": "(iii) lim j ‖ Φ j ‖ 2 ,q = 0",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1331088571428571,
        "y0": 0.3616478098574821,
        "x1": 0.8672607275006454,
        "y1": 0.37573966448931123
      },
      "text": "Proof. · Step 1: we first notice that for every ε > 0 there exists t 0 such that if | t | ≤ t 0 then",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "formula",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.42292302521008396,
        "y0": 0.3879365172209026,
        "x1": 0.5774475810084033,
        "y1": 0.4036906947743468
      },
      "text": "",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.13250334453781504,
        "y0": 0.4177228473871734,
        "x1": 0.8672603073325781,
        "y1": 0.46623861935866984
      },
      "text": "where we use the notation ( K ) t = { p ∈ R n | d ( p, K ) ≤ t } , for the outer parallel set. Indeed, let us assume by contradiction that there exist ε 0 > 0 and points y k ∈ u -1 ( t k ) with lim k t k = 0 such that",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "formula",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.37572947899159653,
        "y0": 0.46532403503562947,
        "x1": 0.6248416146218487,
        "y1": 0.48234289489311166
      },
      "text": "",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.13250242016806718,
        "y0": 0.49190886686460805,
        "x1": 0.8708753472268909,
        "y1": 0.5209822743467933
      },
      "text": "As Ω is bounded, up to a subsequence, we may assume that y k converge to some point ¯ y ∈ Ω . The continuity of u gives u (¯ y ) = 0 , so that ¯ y ∈ u -1 (0) . On the other hand,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "formula",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.429982917647059,
        "y0": 0.5343023129453681,
        "x1": 0.5705913053781515,
        "y1": 0.5511787499999999
      },
      "text": "",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1325042117647062,
        "y0": 0.5661606483372922,
        "x1": 0.32748682528140394,
        "y1": 0.5791297802850356
      },
      "text": "which is a contradiction.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "list",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1331085411764708,
        "y0": 0.5822649238717339,
        "x1": 0.8672605498542962,
        "y1": 0.6285658165083136
      },
      "text": "Step 2: We now want to extend the non-degeneracy property of the gradient of u to the functions u j on their level sets u -1 j (0) . We notice that by uniform convergence and by the previous step, for every ε > 0 there exist t 0 > 0 and j 0 such that",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "formula",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.3029236672268909,
        "y0": 0.6407631205463182,
        "x1": 0.8694712171951396,
        "y1": 0.6594924673396674
      },
      "text": "",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.13310897815126058,
        "y0": 0.6726214559382422,
        "x1": 0.8113751842896657,
        "y1": 0.6867133105700711
      },
      "text": "On the other hand, ∇ u is uniformly continuous in Ω so there exists α 0 > 0 such that",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "formula",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.27831919663865556,
        "y0": 0.6984300059382422,
        "x1": 0.7222547742857143,
        "y1": 0.7290585213776721
      },
      "text": "",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.13310885714285714,
        "y0": 0.7391775485748219,
        "x1": 0.23858374534410093,
        "y1": 0.7521466805225653
      },
      "text": "In particular,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "formula",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.3622181008403361,
        "y0": 0.7518741983372921,
        "x1": 0.6383562700840335,
        "y1": 0.7825027019002375
      },
      "text": "",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.13250447058823525,
        "y0": 0.7873482492874109,
        "x1": 0.6006149148295414,
        "y1": 0.8014401039192399
      },
      "text": "Also, ∇ u j uniformly converge to ∇ u , so for j large enough",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "formula",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.36141134453781504,
        "y0": 0.8142971437054631,
        "x1": 0.6389606398319326,
        "y1": 0.8449255047505938
      },
      "text": "",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1325039999999999,
        "y0": 0.8548245932304038,
        "x1": 0.8696329024634688,
        "y1": 0.8920812796912114
      },
      "text": "From the previous estimates, we get |∇ u j | ( x ) > 0 for every x ∈ u -1 j (0) and j large enough, which implies that the sets u -1 j (0) are C 1 ,s hypersurfaces.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    }
